+## 1. Constraint and catalog-evidence contract
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add the optional closed-vocabulary `flange_subtype` field to normal and golden query constraints; update both structured-extraction prompts and verify mocked extraction/schema tests accept recognized values while generic flanges remain unset.
+- [ ] 1.2 Implement deterministic query normalization and candidate subtype interpretation from affirmative name, article, and property evidence only; verify unit tests cover weld-neck/butt-weld, flat, loose, and counter wording, plus generic flange and generic welded-connection non-inference.
+- [ ] 1.3 Extend normal matching checks, strict golden evaluation, sanitizer unsupported-constraint handling, and product snapshots for the tri-state subtype result; verify focused tests distinguish matching subtype (`PASS`), known mismatch (`FAIL`), and missing evidence (`UNKNOWN`).
+
+## 2. Narrow final-match safeguard
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add a final-result check after reranking that applies only when the original query explicitly requires a recognized flange subtype; convert a selected contradictory or unverified flange into the existing non-match result with a diagnostic reason, and verify mocked matcher tests cover both outcomes.
+- [ ] 2.2 Verify regression behavior for a generic flange query and a non-flange query: their retrieval calls, reranker input/order, selected candidate, and status remain unchanged; add focused tests without altering retrieval, RRF, or reranker configuration.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run focused constraint, golden-rules, and matcher tests, then run `python -m pytest -q`; resolve implementation/test failures without broadening subtype inference or adding catalog/index changes.

